INDUSTRIAL PROJECT STATEMENT

This repository represents an industrial-style cybersecurity
project demonstrating how organizations can design and deploy a
secure Threat Intelligence Sharing Platform using multiple
cybersecurity technologies.

The project is intended to demonstrate practical cybersecurity
architecture, threat intelligence sharing, security controls,
automation, scalability, and interoperability concepts.

The author considers this project an industrial project created
for learning, demonstration, research, and portfolio purposes.

THIRD-PARTY TECHNOLOGIES

This repository may demonstrate or reference third-party
technologies, frameworks, platforms, libraries, tools, threat
feeds, standards, and services.

Examples include MISP, Docker, Redis, STIX, TAXII, Kali Linux,
CIRCL, DigitalSide, and other technologies referenced in the
project documentation.

